WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.750
- Bing with AI is gonna completely change

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:05.730
what people can expect from search.

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:06.870
We are grounded in the fact

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:09.900
that Google dominates this space.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:12.480
I feel like a new race is starting

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.820
with a complete new platform technology.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.730
I'm excited for the users
to have choice finally

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:19.950
and a real competitive race out there.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:21.990
- [Joanna] Microsoft CEO Satya Nadella

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:25.710
finally thinks he has what
it takes to make Bing happen

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:28.680
and grab some search engine
market share from Google.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.420
His not so secret weapon?

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:33.540
- This all started with us
an OpenAI coming together

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.010
with really a research agenda

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:38.820
on moving the state-of-the-art
of AI forward.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:39.900
- [Joanna] Microsoft is taking

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:42.570
OpenAI's newest artificial
intelligence model

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:45.150
and intertwining it
with Bing's search data

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:46.950
so you can chat with the search engine

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:48.960
and get up to date information.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:51.540
- So the entire point of ChatGPT early on

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:54.870
was to just sort of show
the power of the large model

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:56.730
and the conversational intelligence.

00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:59.310
We now have not only
the current information

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:01.740
that you usually expect
from a search engine,

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.170
but you can then have a full conversation

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:05.730
around that current information

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:08.250
and all the other
information that came before.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:10.500
- On top of the new AI
chat features in Bing,

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:13.260
Microsoft is adding ChatGPT-like features

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:16.110
to its Edge browser, so I came here

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:18.780
to Microsoft's headquarters
in Redmond, Washington

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:21.390
to get a hands-on demo of the new tools

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:23.793
and hear Nadell's thoughts on AI.

00:01:24.896 --> 00:01:26.400
(mouse clicks)
The first big new feature,

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:27.690
Bing Chat.

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:30.210
Incorporated right into
the front page of Bing

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:32.670
will be an "ask me anything" box.

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:34.770
Type in your query, say,

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:39.770
the biggest winners of the 2023 Grammys,

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:42.090
because I did not have time to watch it.

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:44.580
And up pops your usual search results,

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:48.150
which Nadella says has
also been improved with AI.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:50.692
But more interesting is this new chat box

00:01:50.692 --> 00:01:54.060
that will start typing out
an answer to the question.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:56.910
As it answers it also includes citations

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:59.370
so you know where the
information is coming from.

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:02.970
- It allows me to then
have a full-on conversation

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:04.530
around all the search data.

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:06.990
So yes, it's annotated,
it's about being able

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:09.870
to create even the links
back to all the publishers,

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:12.120
so this is just search, just better.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.560
- The system took about a minute

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:16.260
to return a list of
the top Grammy winners.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:20.430
Not exactly fast, but you can
tell it to stop responding.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:23.190
Then you can ask follow up questions like,

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:27.240
do you know if Beyonce is touring?

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:29.340
- Perfect.
- If you're a Beyonce fan,

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:30.173
you might wanna hurry

00:02:30.173 --> 00:02:32.130
and get your tickets before they're gone.

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:33.420
Like ChatGPT,

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:36.780
you can ask it non-search
type things too, like,

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:39.300
write 10 questions

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:41.820
for Satya Nadella

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:43.776
about AI.

00:02:43.776 --> 00:02:45.030
(keyboard clicks)

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:47.070
What are the key features and benefits

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:49.650
of New Bing Chat mode, and
how does it leverage AI

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:51.690
to enhance the user experience?

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:55.380
- It really is grounded in search results

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:58.560
and helps me have a very contextual chat

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:00.690
or to be able to get to the right answers.

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:04.657
- Satya Bing said or AI Satya said,

00:03:04.657 --> 00:03:06.667
"The New Bing chat mode leverages AI

00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:10.590
"to understand the
user's intent, context,"

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:11.737
you said context,

00:03:11.737 --> 00:03:14.587
"and preferences to
provide relevant visual,

00:03:14.587 --> 00:03:16.530
"logical, and actionable responses."

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:17.910
- I love the AI Satya.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:18.960
- [Joanna] But while these may seem

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:20.760
like fun and games in these demos,

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:23.940
there are of course real
misuses of this technology.

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:27.540
- We have a lot of practice
in thinking about safety.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:30.900
AI is only good if it is
being used in the real world,

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:34.140
understanding, learning human preferences,

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:35.730
and our intent is to do that,

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:38.880
which is to put stuff
out there with safety,

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:40.470
but at the same time realizing

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:42.660
that we are going to have
to think about safety

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:46.710
as an ongoing responsibility,
not a one-time responsibility.

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:48.570
- He also told me there
are guardrails in place

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:52.093
to prevent harmful content,
hate speech, and more.

00:03:52.093 --> 00:03:52.926
(mouse clicks)

00:03:52.926 --> 00:03:55.470
The second big feature,
Microsoft Edge integration.

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:58.440
The Microsoft Edge browser
will now have a Bing sidebar

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:00.870
where you can ask it to
summarize a webpage you're on

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:03.000
or ask it to generate text.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.190
For instance, I asked it to,

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:09.900
so I wanna write a letter to Satya Nadella

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:13.020
thanking him for his time.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:15.060
Then I was able to tell
it I wanted it written

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:19.237
in an enthusiastic tone
in email form and short.

00:04:19.237 --> 00:04:22.070
(keyboard clicks)

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:23.843
It knows.
- That's pretty good.

00:04:23.843 --> 00:04:24.900
- That's pretty good.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:28.290
There's a lot of fear that
AI is gonna take our jobs,

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:29.700
replace us.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:33.120
Is that unfounded and how
do you think about tools

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:35.940
like Bing now and how we
use it in the job market?

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:39.930
- Like, I think of this as
at the foundational level

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:42.480
going to help us do our jobs better,

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:46.230
reduce some of the drudgery
in some of our jobs,

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:48.150
whether it's in coding or in writing

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:52.320
or in automating a workflow
or searching for information.

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:53.550
So at the fundamental level,

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:55.680
I think we need a productivity boost.

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:57.870
I feel it'll create more jobs.

00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:01.320
The barriers to knowledge
work will come down.

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:04.050
So, I mean, the unintended consequences

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:05.850
around labor market shifts
are always something

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:08.550
we need to be mindful
of, but I don't subscribe

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:12.810
to this zero sum or one
lump of labor fallacy,

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:15.570
and I think that we are going
to have new jobs get created

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:17.370
and more job opportunities.

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:19.110
- And it sounds like more time, right?

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:20.310
- For sure, for sure.

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:21.570
- We outsource some of this.

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:24.390
So I outsourced some of my
question writing to this.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.100
It freed up a little bit more of my time

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:27.150
to do something else.

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:29.610
- And, but you are still in
the loop and you're in charge

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:32.010
because you get to accept the draft.

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:33.510
That's kind of one of
the metaphors I have,

00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:36.330
is pretty much all computer
interaction going forward,

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:37.740
you'll start with a draft.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:40.560
That doesn't mean you don't
get to inspect the draft

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:45.560
or proof the draft and
redefine and edit the draft.

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:46.703
- The question is,

00:05:46.703 --> 00:05:49.230
which company will
write that draft for us?

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:51.720
Will it be Microsoft with tools like this,

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:55.290
or Google, which owns 90% of
the search engine market share,

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:57.570
and, right before my
interview with Mr. Nadella,

00:05:57.570 --> 00:06:00.660
announced Bard, its
similar AI chat feature

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:03.630
that will come to its own search engine?

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:06.300
How are you thinking
about monetizing this?

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:09.120
- The last time I checked
software, I mean, it's a search

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:13.950
was the most profitable category
there is on planet Earth,

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:17.160
so therefore all I need
is a few more users,

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:18.780
and someone else that I'm competing in

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:20.790
has to keep all of their users

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:22.380
and all of their gross margin, right?

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:24.210
So I love, I'm looking forward to that.

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:26.430
- So no plans to charge for New Bing.

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:28.770
It's really advertising
model all the way through.

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:31.710
- We'll start there and
if there are other models,

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:35.190
there may be other models,
but there is enough surplus,

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:36.270
let me put it this way,

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:40.410
there is so much surplus
that goes to one place

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:43.230
which I think would be nice
if it was evenly distributed.

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:44.610
- What about Microsoft Office?

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:45.630
- Just stay tuned.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:49.350
I fully expect us and to
introduce these capabilities,

00:06:49.350 --> 00:06:51.870
quite frankly, across the
length and breadth of Microsoft.

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:52.970
- What about this guy?

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:56.610
- Oh, you know, it's sort
of like it was early,

00:06:56.610 --> 00:06:59.670
and so we get to redefine
it for the AI age

00:06:59.670 --> 00:07:01.140
and it's gonna be very useful.

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:02.250
- So is he coming back?

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:04.380
- He'll come back in a
variety of different ways.

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:05.970
I think I'm most excited about Bing

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:08.640
as the real incarnation of Clippy.

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:11.370
- Okay, but no actual, like, popup?

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:13.890
- I think we have much
better design mechanisms

00:07:13.890 --> 00:07:17.460
to do what Clippy aspired
to do back in the day.

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:19.050
- Does Clippy haunt your dreams?

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:19.883
- Not really.

00:07:19.883 --> 00:07:23.070
It's probably the thing that
was the most fun character

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:24.990
Microsoft introduced, which, you know,

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:26.040
think about it, right?

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:28.650
We have been on a 30-year
journey to perfect it,

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:32.896
so I'm excited to be here in
2023 launching Bing with AI.

00:07:32.896 --> 00:07:35.479
(upbeat music)

